ssucc}

sless x^{
ssucc
ssucc
ssucc} 
sless \dots
\]
We call this subset the \emph{block of~$x$} and write it as $[x]$. It
has no least and no greatest !!{element}. It can be characterized as
the set of those $y \in \Domain{M}$ such that, for some standard~$n$,
$x 
splus n = y$ or $y 
splus n = x$.
